-- `format(ms)`: the largest units first, separated by spaces. `0` is `"0s"`.
+- `parse(text)`: milliseconds from a duration made of `d`, `h`, `m`, `s` and
+  `ms` parts, e.g. `parse("2d4h")` is `187200000`. Throws `TypeError` on empty
+  input and `SyntaxError` on anything else it cannot read.
+- `format(ms, options?)`: the largest units first, separated by spaces, hours
+  at most. `0` is `"0s"`. Pass `{ days: true }` to render days:
+  `format(93600000, { days: true })` is `"1d 2h"`. `options` must be an object
