@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# ADR-001: Keep `UNITS` unchanged; add separate `DAY_UNITS` table
+
+- Status: proposed
+- Change: add-days-unit
+- Date: 2026-10-06
+
+## Context
+`format` builds its output from the shared `UNITS` constant. Consumers persist and compare `format` strings, so the default output must stay byte-identical (REQ-duration-formatting-001). The config archive rule warns before modifying `UNITS`.
+
+## Decision
+Leave `UNITS` as is. Add `DAY_UNITS = Object.freeze({ d: 86400000, ...UNITS })`. `parse` looks units up in `DAY_UNITS`. `format` iterates `UNITS` by default and `DAY_UNITS` only when `options.days === true`. `PATTERN` becomes `/(\d+)(ms|d|h|m|s)/g`, with `ms` kept before `m`.
+
+## Alternatives
+- Add `d` to `UNITS` and filter it in default `format`: the default output would then depend on a filter, and the protected constant would be touched.
+- Second full literal table: duplicates the sub-day unit values.
+
+## Consequences
+Default output is identical by construction, because it runs the same code over the same object. One extra frozen constant. Fully reversible.
