+# ADR-002: Strict `format` options contract
+
+- Status: proposed
+- Change: add-days-unit
+- Date: 2026-10-06
+
+## Context
+The proposal said falsy `days` keeps default output. The spec (REQ-duration-formatting-005) chose a stricter rule. This option is new public API, so it is the cheapest point to fix its validation.
+
+## Decision
+`ms` is validated first. `options` must be `undefined` or a plain object (prototype `Object.prototype` or `null`), otherwise `TypeError`. `options.days` is read once and must be `boolean` or `undefined`, otherwise `TypeError`; `undefined` means `false`. Unknown keys are ignored and `options` is never mutated. `FormatOptions { days?: boolean }` is exported in `index.d.ts`.
+
+## Alternatives
+- Truthy/falsy coercion: `{ days: 'false' }` would silently render days and corrupt persisted strings.
+- Loose `typeof === 'object'` check: contradicts "plain object" in the spec. Loosening later is non-breaking; tightening later would be breaking.
+
+## Consequences
+Misuse fails loudly. Cross-realm option objects (e.g. from `vm`) are rejected, which is a minor cost and can be relaxed in a later minor release.
